[i][DEMO GIF SLOT — loadout-to-sidearms clip goes here at publish][/i]

One mental model for [b]Combat Extended[/b] loadouts and [b]Simple Sidearms[/b] memory. The CE loadout is the shared template; each pawn's SS sidearm memory is the living copy of it.

[h1]What it does[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Loadout weapons become sidearms.[/b] Single-count weapons in a CE loadout are auto-remembered by assigned pawns. First in the list sets the main-weapon role (default ranged / preferred melee); the rest are backups. Remove a weapon from the loadout and it's forgotten — and CE then cleans it out of inventories. The loadout is the authority: a weapon def it lists is managed by it whoever remembered that weapon first. Defs the loadout never lists are never touched.
[*][b]Ammo is Combat Extended's job.[/b] Add the ammo to the loadout and CE keeps the pawn stocked to that count — the same mechanism it uses for everything else, and it works whether or not the weapon itself is declared.
[/list]

[h1]Requires[/h1]
Harmony, Combat Extended, Simple Sidearms, and the [url=https://github.com/eebette/CombatExtended-SimpleSidearms-Compatibility-Patch]CombatExtended-SimpleSidearms Compatibility Patch[/url] (the core of this suite). Load after all four (auto-sorted).

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*]Safe to add mid-save. Removing mid-save leaves only inert SS sidearm memories plus a one-time load warning — no corruption.
[*]Reconciliation runs on CE's own loadout cadence; the Assign tab's "update now" button applies changes instantly.
[/list]

